WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.701
-Our next guest
has his new stand-up special,

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:05.868
"Thank You China,"
available now on YouTube.

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:07.701
Making his "Tonight Show" debut,

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:10.701
please welcome the very funny
Nimesh Patel.

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:13.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:18.067
♪♪

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:19.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:22.000
-Hi, hi, hi.
Thank you guys so much.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.400
My parents
caught me smoking weed

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.801
on a YouTube livestream
at age 35.

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:31.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:32.734
My dad called me immediately.

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:34.534
"Nimesh, what are you smoking?"

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.100
I said, "It's weed, Dad."

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.801
He said, "you need to quit."

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:39.968
I said, "Okay, Dad,
I'll quit smoking weed

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:42.634
when you
quit smoking cigarettes."

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:43.868
He said the most dad thing ever.

00:00:43.868 --> 00:00:46.534
He said,
"I'm not gonna argue with you."

00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:48.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:50.100
I said, "Yeah, Dad,
we just had the argument.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.000
You lost."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.200
"It's fine.
Take the 'L,' bro."

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.234
He said, "I'll get you back."
Then he hung up.

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:58.734
And a few minutes later,
I start seeing all the dislikes

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:00.701
on my YouTube videos
go up by one.

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:04.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:07.067
And then I got a call
from my mom.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.901
"Nimesh, what are you smoking?"

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:11.667
And she's mad religious,
so I said, "Hindu Kush?"

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:13.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:15.334
She said, "Don't get smart.
Is that weed?

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:17.434
You need to stop.
It's illegal."

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:20.267
I said, "Illegal?
So is not paying taxes

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:23.033
on that all-cash liquor store
we got going on, but..."

00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:24.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.634
"...I won't tell if you don't."

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:27.968
Without missing a beat,
she says,

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:29.567
"Nimesh, the store's
in your name.

00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:32.901
You don't pay taxes."
[ Laughter, audience "Ohhs" ]

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:35.467
Snitching on myself.

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:37.634
And then, she said,
"Nimesh, you need to quit.

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:39.467
You have asthma."

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:42.367
I said, "Mom, I read
when I was high

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:45.601
that weed is a bronchodilator."

00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:48.634
And she goes, "Oh.
So now you want to be a doctor?

00:01:48.634 --> 00:01:52.567
Hm, that's cute."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:54.234
Speaking of which --
Speaking of which,

00:01:54.234 --> 00:01:57.534
clap if you believe that
Americans deserve healthcare.

00:01:57.534 --> 00:02:03.467
Clap if you believe Americans --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:03.467 --> 00:02:05.501
You don't?
Me neither.

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:06.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:10.234
I think we need it,
but I don't think we deserve it.

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:12.434
I know I don't deserve
healthcare.

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:14.334
A few years ago,
I discovered exactly

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:17.767
how much weed I need to smoke
to have an asthma attack.

00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:20.267
I had an asthma attack.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:23.701
I went to a Kanye West concert
back when it was okay to do.

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:25.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.701
I smoked four joints in an hour.

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:29.701
And then his song "I Am a God"
came on,

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:32.501
and I was like, "I'm not, Kanye.
I have to go to the hospital."

00:02:32.501 --> 00:02:33.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.868 --> 00:02:36.367
And I called an Uber
to the hospital

00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:37.968
'cause an ambulance is $600,

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:40.267
and I'm not gonna die a sucker,
you know?

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:41.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:42.400
Get to the hospital.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.467
NYU Langone in Cobble Hill,
Brooklyn.

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:47.634
And now I have asthma,
so I know exactly what I need.

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:50.100
"Doctor,
I'm having an asthma attack."

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:51.801
"You're having
an asthma attack."

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:54.100
"I need Albuterol nebulizer."

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:55.434
"You need Albuterol nebulizer."

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:56.601
I'm like,
"Is this self-checkout?

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:58.667
What's happening right now?"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:01.300
"Just give me my medicine.
He's like, "you'll be fine."

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:04.267
Then he shuffles away
in his Ferragamo loafers.

00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:07.000
And then in comes a nurse
who has a menu of all

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.267
the other stuff I could get

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:11.067
since I've stopped in
at Casa de NYU.

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:13.267
Blood work, EKG.

00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:15.634
The chef recommended X-ray.

00:03:15.634 --> 00:03:17.400
But I don't present
as a 30-year-old Indian man

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.567
having a heart attack.

00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:20.534
What they're doing is running up
the insurance tab

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:23.200
because insurance will just pay
whatever the hospital says.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.334
And whatever they don't pay,
they pass on to you.

00:03:25.334 --> 00:03:27.334
But, luckily,
I said the magic words.

00:03:27.334 --> 00:03:29.868
I said,
"I don't have insurance."

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:31.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:34.000
This lady
threw an inhaler at me

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.267
and was like, "Get out,
you wheezy, broke loser."

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:37.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:37.734 --> 00:03:40.200
"Jesus."

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.601
Sure.

00:03:42.601 --> 00:03:44.767
[ Laughs ]

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:46.100
You're clapping
for poor healthcare.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:48.267
That's great, that's great.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:50.267
In and out
in an hour and a half.

00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:51.934
Two weeks later, get the bill.

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:54.200
$6,000.
[ Audience groans ]

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.567
Yeah.
I had another asthma attack.

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:56.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.567 --> 00:03:59.100
[ Wheezing ]

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:03.100
$6,000 for an hour and a half
and not a single orgasm.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.801 --> 00:04:07.934
But luckily,
I was raised by Indian people

00:04:07.934 --> 00:04:10.601
who taught me that the price
is never the price

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:13.267
until you talk about the price.

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:15.667
I called the hospital.
I said, "Listen,

00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:18.868
I'm not giving you $6,000."
They said, "Why not?"

00:04:18.868 --> 00:04:24.334
I said, "Well, for one, you
already gave me the medicine.

00:04:24.334 --> 00:04:27.100
Two, I don't have $6,000."

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.901
Now I had $6,000,
but I also know a little bit

00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:31.300
about the healthcare system.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.334
I know that if that you get sick
at the beginning of the year

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:36.300
like I did, every hospital
has this giant pool of money

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.000
they have to give away
for free care

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.901
in order to stay non-profit.
Sidebar, if you get sick

00:04:41.901 --> 00:04:43.501
and have to go to hospital
in like December,

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:45.501
just hold on, okay?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.501 --> 00:04:48.100
Just hold on for dear life.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.400
And I know this
because I'm talking to them.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.133
"Listen, I don't have $6,000.
I can't give you $6,000.

00:04:52.133 --> 00:04:53.934
I don't have $6,000."

00:04:53.934 --> 00:04:56.767
They literally said,
"How much do you have?"

00:04:56.767 --> 00:04:58.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.501 --> 00:05:01.667
Did I call the mob?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.300
"I got nothing. You can break
my knees if you want.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.167
I'm not giving you $6,000."

00:05:05.167 --> 00:05:06.734
They're like, "All right,
Mr. Patel, no need to be upset.

00:05:06.734 --> 00:05:09.901
Listen, if you don't have
$6,000, you don't owe us $6,000.

00:05:09.901 --> 00:05:12.234
But if you have $6,000,
and you're not paying it,

00:05:12.234 --> 00:05:14.167
you might be taking $6,000
out of the pocket

00:05:14.167 --> 00:05:16.167
of someone who truly can't pay."

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:18.868
I said, "Don't hate the player.
Hate the game."

00:05:18.868 --> 00:05:20.667
Click!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.667 --> 00:05:22.601
Thank you guys so much.
I mean that.

00:05:22.601 --> 00:05:24.267
Thank you.

00:05:24.267 --> 00:05:26.734
♪♪

00:05:26.734 --> 00:05:28.934
-Come on.
-Thanks, bud.

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:32.767
-Nimesh Patel!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:32.767 --> 00:05:36.133
"Thank You China"
is available now on YouTube.

